      "description": "Watch York City LFC vs Bristol Rovers highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The League Two stage was set for a compelling encounter as York City faced off against Bristol Rovers . With both teams eager to climb the table, the atmosphere was thick with anticipation as the referee signaled the start of play. Visitors Take the Initiative In a match played on August 15, 2026 , it was Bristol Rovers who struck the first blow. In the 30th minute, Clinton Mola found the back of the net following a clever assist from Fabrizio Cavegn . The visitors managed to maintain their discipline throughout the remainder of the first half, frustrating the home side and heading into the locker rooms with a 1-0 lead, despite a late first-half substitution that saw Alex Newby enter the fray for York City . Second Half Surge The restart saw a transformed York City side that wasted no time in asserting themselves. The equalizer arrived in the 60th minute when Alex Newby , proving to be an inspired substitution, scored thanks to a setup by Joe Grey . Moments later, the home fans were in raptures as Harry Boyes completed the turnaround in the 63rd minute, clinical finishing following an assist from Ollie Pearce . The game grew increasingly physical as the clock ticked down, with Oliver Banks and Morgan Williams both entering the referee's book. Penalty Drama and Boyes’ Decisive Strike Late drama unfolded when Bristol Rovers were awarded a penalty in the 79th minute. Tommy Leigh stepped up and coolly converted from the spot to make it 2-2. However, the parity lasted less than sixty seconds. In the 80th minute, Alex Newby turned provider for Harry Boyes , who netted his second goal of the match to restore the lead. Despite late pressure and several tactical substitutions from both managers, York City held firm through six minutes of stoppage time to claim a thrilling 3-2 victory."
